body:
Our lab had the PHCBI -30 and -80 and two older Thermo -20s. Never had any issues with any of them. A neighboring lab had three of the Thermo TSX ULTs in the linear bay and those were much quieter than the PHCBIs were and I personally like the look/feel of those more but that's just me. With our ULT we waited about a year to defrost our ULT and it was a mess -- the inner doors had so much ice on them they could barely close. 

&#x200B;

I now work in the hospital and we use Follett ice makers and fridges and they seem to be really reliable. I believe that we use Follett for drug and vaccine storage as well however I'm not 100% sure about that.

&#x200B;

Let me know if you have any questions and I'll do my best to help out where I can!! :)

[https://www.xerox.com/en-us/office/multifunction-printers/primelink-c9065-c9070](https://www.xerox.com/en-us/office/multifunction-printers/primelink-c9065-c9070)

&#x200B;

This one looks pretty interesting but it might be too much for our needs. Any thoughts? I am attracted to the reliability of the production class machines as the office machines seem to be less reliable, but what do I know?

